  "text": " I said no. Prue took the book. She held it in both capped hands against her chest, the way Loveday Hoskin had held a jar. I'd have been Ivy's catcher. I'd have been good. I'd have been the girl from Meridian on Ivy's crew who used to be Rowan's cord. She looked at Kiva. I'm on a sheet, my own with my name on the hem in ink. I'm going back to the crook line and I'm going to find three people who've never heard of the pit and I'm going to catch for them and nobody's going to say whose I was. She held the book tighter. I'm not grateful to anybody. I'm only good. I'd like that written in the book on the first page I write on.",
